{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>יִמְצָאֵהוּ בְּאֶרֶץ מִדְבָּר וּבְתֹהוּ וְגוֹ׳.</b> It appears that the verse intends according to the statement of Amram, of blessed memory (Berakhot 9:), that Israel did not leave Egypt until they made it like a מצולה (deep) that has no fish, etc., and they further said (Likkutei Torah, VaYera) that if Israel had lingered in Egypt they would have been absorbed there forever, for they would have entered the fiftieth gate of impurity. Therefore it says יִמְצָאֵהוּ בְּאֶרֶץ — in a land that is מִדְבָּר, meaning desolate with nothing whatsoever in it. And for this reason it did not say יִמְצָאֵהוּ בַּמִּדְבָּר but rather בְּאֶרֶץ מִדְבָּר. And understand this." "<b>And it further says</b> that not only was the land a desert without any spark of holiness, but it was תֹּהוּ יְלֵל יְשִׁימוֹן — meaning filled with filth and impurity. And you will find that they said in the Zohar (part 1, 16:) that תֹּהוּ is an aspect of one קליפה, and likewise יְלֵל יְשִׁימוֹן, which are aspects of evil — a place denuded of good and filled with evil. Therefore ה׳ סִבְּבוֹ — meaning, an expression of guarding — and it says it in the future tense, meaning that the guarding He performed for him did not cease and will yet be perpetual. And the intention in this is that He brought them out from that evil place so they would not be absorbed there; further, even in that very place itself, when HaShem brought the plagues upon Egypt, He was guarding them, according to what is said (Exodus 9:4) ״וּמִמִּקְנֵה יִשְׂרָאֵל״ etc., ״בְּאֶרֶץ גֹּשֶׁן״ etc. (Exodus 9:26), ״וּלְכָל בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל הָיָה אוֹר״ etc. (Exodus 10:23), ״וְלֹא יִתֵּן הַמַּשְׁחִית״ etc. (Exodus 12:23), and this is what it says: ״יְסוֹבְבֶנְהוּ״." "And His saying <b>יְבוֹנְנֵהוּ</b> — meaning, through giving them the Torah, which is the source of understanding, for through this ״יִצְּרֶנְהוּ כְּאִישׁוֹן עֵינוֹ״, according to what is said (Proverbs 2:11) ״תְּבוּנָה תִנְצְרֶכָּה״. And His saying ״כְּאִישׁוֹן עֵינוֹ״ — as the prophet said (Zechariah 2:12) ״כִּי הַנּוֹגֵעַ בָּכֶם כְּנוֹגֵעַ בְּבָבַת עֵינוֹ״. And the intention in this: just as the eye does not tolerate the touch of a person's finger upon it, the reason being that the body of the finger is turbid while the eye is pure, and the spiritual does not tolerate the physical. And this is the sod of the statement of Rashbi (Zohar vol. 2, 211:) who said: Woe to the soul that bears a foreign fire — meaning, the fire through which it is punished is a foreign fire in comparison to the fire of the soul, and therefore you will find there that the soul of the righteous immerses in the fire called נְהַר דִּינוּר — meaning, as long as the fire has not become distanced and not become physicalized, in which case they will not suffer. And understand the sod of these matters." "<b>And this</b> is what it says here: ״כְּאִישׁוֹן עֵינוֹ״ — for they are spiritual and everything outside of them is physical, and therefore [the enemies] would harm and destroy them even through the touch of the turbid, just as the touch of a hand harms the pupil of the eye. And this was after He bequeathed them the Torah, and therefore He prefaced by saying ״יְבוֹנְנֵהוּ״ and only afterward said ״יִצְּרֶנְהוּ כְּאִישׁוֹן עֵינוֹ״. And this is the reason for negative commandments. And understand this:" "<b>Further,</b> it may intend ״יְבוֹנְנֵהוּ יִצְּרֶנְהוּ״ according to their statement, of blessed memory, in tractate Berakhot 54:, that three require guarding, and one of them is a Torah scholar, the reason being that the harmful forces are zealous of the stature of a son of Torah and wage war against him. Therefore it says ״יְבוֹנְנֵהוּ״ — meaning, He gives him the Torah, which is called תְּבוּנָה (Proverbs 2:11); therefore it is upon Him to guard him, as it says ״יִצְּרֶנְהוּ״ etc.:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "The Aramaic phrase וַי לָהּ לְנִשְׁמְתָא דְּסָבְלָא אֶשָּׁא נוּכְרָאָה is translated hyper-literally below per the instruction regarding obscure passages; the commentator himself glosses it in Hebrew immediately after."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:34.065398206Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}